reviews:
I learned the skills in this course:
1. List the tasks so as not to be missed;
2. Sleep and breathing are important for concentration;
3. Create rewards to encourage goals;
4. Create a habit to shape a personality;
5. Benefits of group study;
...

This is a very basic course on Machine Learning. The main drawbacks are: 
(1) the material is old and not updated to reflect new developments in this dynamic subject;
(2) the course is oversimplified and adapted for students who have never dealt with maths or programming;
(3) the assignments and quizes are, with rare exception, trivial and test students' common sense rather than the subject understanding; for example, you can pass the final quiz at 100% without reading or watching the lectures;
(4) the course is badly maintained: some mistakes in lectures and assignments have not been corrected for years, even though they have been pointed out in the discussion forum countless times.
While the Ng's ML course is arguably better than many other Coursera courses, it is very disappointing that Coursera and Stanford hardly made an attempt to improve it.

Wonderful experience with the course under the guidance from Professor Andrew Ng.
1. Course content has covered all related topics and suitable for beginner and experts;
2. All mathmatic knowledge required are introduced and explained in course;
3. Reviews and programming tasks are fine tuned for every course; Some reviews have comments on explaining the details;
4. For me as a rookie, after the course, really feel that I learned a lot and found that there is lot of fun digging into reviews and programming tasks to help understand and also implement the Machine Learning knowledge.
5. Grateful and thank you for providing the course with free source that spread knowledge.
